PRs are merged with a merge commit, never squash or rebase: git notes are attached to commit SHAs, and squash/rebase merges put new SHAs on main, so the notes would be left on commits that are no longer in main's history. Deferred items sit under the phase where they first matter, not in a backlog: VTT under the web app because browsers need it for <track> (SRT covers players); CI under the PyPI package because a release is the first point where a broken install hurts someone other than the author, and its check can only be required in the ruleset after it has run once. Branches use a docs/ prefix for docs-only work, alongside feat/ and fix/.
